    "description"     "[h1]Hello, Comrade![/h1]Tired of digging through `.ini` text files to tweak mod settings, losing your mod setup when a loader updates, or wondering why a save crashed?

[b]Glorious Republic Mod Loader (GRML)[/b] is a modern, easy-to-use launcher and in-game [b]F9[/b] settings hub for [b]Workers & Resources: Soviet Republic[/b] ([i]SOVIET64.exe 1.2.0.9+[/i]). It keeps your saves backed up, lets you configure mods with sliders and toggles (even in-game), and helps your mods survive game updates.

[b]Version:[/b] v{VERSION} (Alpha) | [b]Source & Releases:[/b] [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader]GitHub Repository[/url]

[b]Alpha Notice:[/b] This is an early public [b]Alpha[/b]. While GRML automatically backs up your saves before launch, please still keep manual backups of important republics and report any bugs on [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader/issues]GitHub Issues[/url].

[h1]How to Use (Step-by-Step)[/h1]Because GRML is a standalone launcher (`GloriousRepublicModLoader.exe`), simply clicking Play in Steam will [b]not[/b] open it automatically:

[list=1]
[*] Subscribe to [b]Glorious Republic Mod Loader (GRML)[/b] here on Steam Workshop.
[*] Open its Workshop folder in your Steam Library:
[code]<Your Steam Library>\steamapps\workshop\content\784150\{PUBLISHED_FILE_ID}\[/code]
[*] Run [b]GloriousRepublicModLoader.exe[/b] (Tip: create a Desktop shortcut or add it to Steam as a Non-Steam Game).
[*] Turn on the mods you want, adjust their settings if needed, and click [b]Launch WRSR[/b] (or [b]Continue <SaveName>[/b] to jump straight into your latest save).
[*] Press [b]F9[/b] anytime in-game to open [b]GRML Mod Settings[/b]!
[/list]
All your settings, playlists, mod configs, and save backups live safely in [code]%LOCALAPPDATA%\GRML[/code], so Workshop updates never wipe your setup.

[h1]Fewer Broken Mods After Game Updates[/h1]Normally, when *Workers & Resources* receives a patch, native DLL mods can stop working until every individual mod author updates their mod.

[b]GRML's Offsets System is designed to prevent that:[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Centralized per-version offsets:[/b] GRML stores the game memory offsets for each supported WRSR version inside the launcher (`grml_offsets.ini`).
[*] [b]One-click updates:[/b] When a new WRSR patch drops, you can click [b]Update Offsets (OTA)[/b] in Settings to grab the latest offset definitions without waiting for a full mod-by-mod rebuild.
[*] [b]Mods keep working:[/b] As soon as GRML has the offsets for the new game version, most compatible mods should continue working automatically—without each mod needing its own update.
[*] [b]Pre-launch safety check:[/b] Before launching, GRML checks every enabled mod against your game version (`Ready` / `Degraded` / `Needs Offset Update`) and lets you temporarily disable affected mods in one click.
[/list]

[h1]What You Get as a Player[/h1][list]
[*] [b]Visual Mod Settings (Launcher & In-Game F9):[/b] Adjust mod options with sliders, toggles, and dropdowns instead of editing `.ini` files—even for older mods that only include a plain `.ini`.
[*] [b]Automatic Savegame Backups:[/b] Automatically backs up your saves before launching into per-game-version folders (so switching WRSR versions never overwrites backups), with a live progress bar and configurable retention limit (default: 3 per version).
[*] [b]Save Inspector & Missing Mod Finder:[/b] Check any save's date, map template, and Workshop dependencies—and copy missing Workshop IDs or open their Steam pages in one click.
[*] [b]Playlists & Safe Defaults:[/b] Newly discovered mods start disabled until you turn them on. Save your favorite mod combinations as one-click Playlists.
[*] [b]Non-Destructive Asset Overrides:[/b] Layer texture/model override folders or `.zip` packs with drag-and-drop priority without ever touching your original game files.
[*] [b]Direct-to-Save Launch & Faster Startup:[/b] Boot straight into your latest save while skipping the 9.5s intro logo delay.
[*] [b]CrashGuard Diagnostics:[/b] If the game crashes, GRML points out which mod faulted so you can disable it in one click.
[/list]

[h1]Works With Your Existing Mods[/h1]GRML automatically finds your subscribed Steam Workshop (`784150`) mods, local `plugins/`, and `workshop_wip/` mods—and stays [b]100% compatible[/b] with existing [b]RML[/b], [b]TesmioLoader[/b], and standalone DLL mods.

[h1]For Mod Authors[/h1]Want your mod to use GRML's shared offsets, automatic `F9` / launcher settings UI, or pure-C plugin SDK? Check out the developer docs on GitHub:
[list]
[*] [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader/blob/main/docs/PLUGIN_SDK.md]Plugin SDK (grml_api.h)[/url]
[*] [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader/blob/main/docs/DECLARATIVE_UI_SCHEMA.md]Declarative UI Schema (.ui.yaml / .ui.json)[/url]
[*] [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader/blob/main/docs/OFFSETS_AND_SIGNATURES.md]Offsets & Signatures Guide[/url] & [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader/blob/main/docs/OFFSET_CATALOG.md]Offset Catalog[/url]
[*] [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md]Architecture Overview[/url] & [url=https://github.com/ZydraHydra/GloriousRepublicModLoader/blob/main/docs/HOOKING_AND_PERFORMANCE_RULES.md]Hooking & Performance Rules[/url]
[/list]{CHANGELOG_SECTION}"
    "language"        "english"
    "changenote"      "{CHANGENOTE}"
}
